// The state schema: a small subset of WIT describing a component's state
// record and its message buckets.
//
// Pure and target-agnostic like viewgen/ and cli/: source text in -> a typed
// StateDef out, never touching the filesystem. viewgen/ threads the result
// through view generation; cmd/main does the I/O.
//
// Names resolve against the WIT *AST* (@wit.parse), not the resolver
// (@wit.resolve): tutuca's marker types (`any`, `text-set`, a sibling
// component) have no WIT declaration to resolve against, and doing the
// lookup here keeps the user's byte offsets exact — nothing is prepended to
// their source, so a parse error still points where they wrote it.
import {
  "mizchi/wit",
  "moonbitlang/core/debug",
  "moonbitlang/core/json",
}

// The emitted WIT is checked by feeding it BACK through the parser: a
// document wit-bindgen would reject is worse than none.
import {
  "mizchi/wit",
} for "test"
